    Descriptions draw on the Chipedge and Futurense embedded-versus-VLSI comparisons, the Chitkara University mechatronics guide and the Electronics Sector Skills Council packs. The first two are sold by training firms and the third by a college, so treat their salary claims as marketing.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">A cheap test before you commit</p>
    <p>
      Write a small block of Verilog and a testbench, then write a small firmware project that reads a sensor.
      Some people know within a few weeks which one they keep returning to; others need a couple of months. Free simulators and a basic board are enough.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="ism">The semiconductor push, read carefully</h2>

  <p>
    India's chip policy is the biggest reason people ask about VLSI. These are the official facts, followed by what they mean for a fresher.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
